Then we need to allocate dispatch slot (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate) requiring dispatch_ready, candidate_task_profile_linked (still linked), dispatch_slot_available.

Then assign vehicle (already done). Then execute_schedule_dispatch.

Thus for each schedule candidate we need to consume: one operational_constraint (alpha for shift_candidate_alpha, beta for shift_candidate_beta), one operator (same operator can be reused after release? We need to release operator after use? There's release_operator_resource action that makes operator_available again. So we can assign, then after confirm_operator_alignment we could release? But verify_compliance_certificate does not require operator still linked? It only needs operator_alignment_confirmed (which persists) and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. The operator resource may still be linked; but we might need to release later for other candidates. However we only have one operator; we need to use it for both schedule candidates and also for origin/destination availabilities (locking actions need operator_resource). The lock_origin_availability and lock_destination_availability actions require candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource. So we need to link operator to origin/destination availabilities as well. So we need to allocate operator to each candidate sequentially, releasing after each use.

Thus we need to manage operator resource: assign, use for locking, then release.

Similarly for skill_certificate: needed for verify_loading_profile_* actions to get candidate_loading_verified. Those require candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, and either destination_leg_loaded or not. So we need skill_certificate for each candidate to verify loading.

We have only one skill_certificate_alpha. So need to assign, use, release.

Compliance_certificate: needed for assign_compliance_certificate and verify_compliance_certificate. Also needed for establish_clearance actions (they require candidate_compliance_certificate_linked). So we need to link compliance certificate to each candidate before clearance and verification. We have only one compliance_certificate_alpha. So need to assign, use, release.

Equipment_resource: needed for reserve_equipment_resource and confirm_equipment_assignment. We have two equipment resources: alpha and beta. Could assign each to a candidate.

Loading_containers: we have two: alpha and beta. Each schedule candidate already linked to a loading container via init (candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_alpha loading_container_alpha, shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta). So we don't need to link; they are already linked. Good.

